-- check/bad: CK-121. A definition followed by a SEPARATE annotation with a
-- `where` clause: the annotation has no definition (it does not follow
-- one) and repeats the name. Both are the frontend's diagnostics; the checker
-- must add nothing and not fail. Checker v2 panicked (exit 134) in P6: the
-- bodyless annotation has no rigid reading, so no givens, and P6 asserted
-- it had them (`Module.elaborate`).
less x y =
    x < y


less : a, a -> Bool where a.compare : a, a -> Order
